    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d50">

                <pb facs="0056" n="42" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg42"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Conference W and PW/2–2245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">La Paz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-22T15:00:00-04:00">February 22,
                            1945—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:21 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>204. Embassy’s 182, February 17, noon.<anchor n="86" xml:id="d50-f1"/> Colonel
                        Pinto<anchor n="87" xml:id="d50-f2"/> called me to the Foreign Office this
                    noon to say that it has become necessary to modify the assurances he gave me a
                    few days ago. He said the Bolivian Government understands that the Chilean
                    delegation at the Mexico City Conference will introduce proposals looking toward
                    general recognition of the territorial <hi rendition="#italic">status quo</hi>.
                    Inasmuch as acceptance of this scheme would block Bolivia’s rightful claim to an
                    outlet to the Pacific, the Bolivian delegation will, if any such proposal is
                    made at the Conference, assert its views with respect to the port question.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
